pacts with Demon Lords for good eh I mean bad measures. Still not overpowered enough? Then let's go to the True Brujah and Temporis. The explanation why there is still a balance at all is in most cases the same. Because there are only so few (left) of them. Because so many will (try to) destroy them.. Uhm.. okay, that sounds &amp;quot;very plausible&amp;quot;, especially when survival of the fittest is one of the main settings in the game. Temporis controls the time itself. To fight a being which might control time, even in limited ways, is in the best cases difficult. And while all other Clans multiply these with the really powerful disciplines don't, because...?<br /> Manipulation of time and how to not be able to loose fights if you do it brings us back to Mages.<br /> Mages against Vampires or Werewolves.. oh my.. As good as any Sphere might be used as an absolute killer for both. Ok, there are some which are not direct final deadly; but with these you just have to be a bit more creative (like Life against Vampires; go against their meals instead). Against Werewolves it's even worse. So the trick for both might perhaps be the good old principle &amp;quot;kill the Mage first&amp;quot;. If Mages could not also learn manipulation of Correspondence and Time. <br /> ---<br /> Where I have to disagree with most people here is in regard of the Week of Nightmares. I both liked it and saw sense in it; at least if you also see the events in the world of Wraiths. The WoD is a slightly changed mirror of our reality. The reaction taken by the Technocracy are just a logical step with technologies which do exist. Sun mirrors &amp; Nukes. I don't really get why the storm which shielded the Antediluvian could not be stopped with any other Magic means (like: Freeze him eternal in time. Teleport him with Correspondence into the center of Earth or into the Sun. Put some mega-tonnes of indestructible matter on him or just transform his lifeless body into anything you like (have you seen my chick Antediluvian chair yet <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />? Use entropy to impend massive doom and soak any defense he might have (AFTER the roll). Use Prime to draw the power out of the magic/disciplines which power the storm. And these are just ways which first got into my mind.. Oh I forgot, use mind to just let him sleep again. Yes, as an Antediluvian he may use counter magic. But we are talking here over an concentrated effort of the whole damn Technocracy. And if Tradition mages sometimes help out in fighting Marauders &amp; Nephandi, guess what happens if the oldest of the Suckers wake up? But okay, if you also look what happened on the other side of the Shroud with the Wraiths it begins to fit at least a bit better and it also leads to the last trilogy, which is one of mine absolute favorites of all trilogies, both in the WoD as well as without . The only very bad thing was that it also leads to the end of my most loved RP world.. But what an end it was. In good books some or even all Characters die. And in some of the best the Earth or just anything has to die therefore. Never was the saying with one crying and one smiling eye better fitting. But I digressed.<br /> ---<br /> Clanbook Baali.. I can't say I liked it, but it had to stand out of all the other horrors to be &amp;quot;extra evil&amp;quot; and that's not easy to do. Nevertheless it was bad enough that I did not read all the stories, which in other Clanbooks were the part I most enjoyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a couple weeks after I read Clanbook Baali every time I saw a crawling bug I REALLY freaked out...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T11:12:20-07:00","id":1411104,"title":"","content":"Clanbook Baali was good. The intro was a little juvenile and i recognise some people can't deal with that sorta stuff and it's not entirely necessary even for a black dog book (it does set the tone rather well), but it's the best writeup they got.<br /> <br /> I really don't like the idea they've pushed later on which suggests Baali are the vampire equivelent of nephandi or bsds. They might be a bloodline of evil and attrocity, but they don't have inverted souls, it's a very human, religious evil they practice. The embrace is not a caul, apostacy is not a caul. You don't get your soul inverted because the wrong bloodline embraced you. It's a nice in-universe perspective to believe all baali are irredeemable, fundamentally deranged monsters hated by God and damned for all eternity upon embrace regardless of who they are, but it should never be the truth-of-the-universe just because you're uncomfortable with the idea of nuerotypical religious extremists who practice a very foul faith. <br /> <br /> (right, yeah, I'm not going to make the claim that they're all neurotypical, most Baali are going to embrace people who'll fit in, IE high functioning psychopaths, but the Baali also target very moral and faithful people to see them slide, kinda like nosferatu attraction to targeting beautiful people, and people deal with trauma differently. If Baali could just make nice priests evil upon embrace it'd be very shallow and ridiculous. It's far better to have that priest struggle against his new Baali reality as the ordeals he faces take their toll. ) .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T19:15:38-07:00","id":1411288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1398439-worst-wod-idea-you\u2019ve-ever-heard?p=1405540#post1405540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">me, I just wish they'd focus less on the umbra and tried to make the mundane world less mundane,<br /> maybe have some interesting urban mysteries, hiding in plain sight</div> </div> </div> </div>They arguably did this with Chronicles of Darkness, so people on the design teams must have agreed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T00:48:36-07:00","id":1411303,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's that the Baali embrace automatically makes someone evil to the core, it's that the vampire doing the embracing is going to regard anyone who doesn't get with the Yay Evil! program pretty quickly as a failure and a danger to themselves and their agenda. Soft-hearted Baali fledgelings probably have survival rates lower than pacifist shovelheads who try to talk out differences with the packs that embrace them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T02:37:47-07:00","id":1411313,"title":"","content":"Yeah the Mage developers where surprised that people rather have cool Umbra fights then I don\u2019t know dealing with a land lord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T11:07:34-07:00","id":1411837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1398439-worst-wod-idea-you\u2019ve-ever-heard?p=1411303#post1411303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's that the Baali embrace automatically makes someone evil to the core, it's that the vampire doing the embracing is going to regard anyone who doesn't get with the Yay Evil! program pretty quickly as a failure and a danger to themselves and their agenda. Soft-hearted Baali fledgelings probably have survival rates lower than pacifist shovelheads who try to talk out differences with the packs that embrace them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention there's undoubtedly Selection Bias at work with those Embraced in the first place. If your potential sire doesn't think you're Baali material, you wouldn't be targeted for the Embrace to begin with. (Unless the Baali was Embracing you specifically for malicious intent; even then, they'll be working very hard to &quot;correct&quot; your behavior, if they aren't just doing it to get their jollies and then destroy you afterwards). Most of the time, a newly created Baali was assumed to be sufficiently &quot;Baali-like&quot; to warrant being made one, or at least had the qualities that could be molded into a &quot;proper&quot; Baali.<br /> <br /> Obviously, what constitutes &quot;proper&quot; Baali behavior differs from era to era and depends on context. In the past, when Baali were making war on everyone, a person could qualify for becoming a Baali if they simply displayed enough viciousness. (Although, as illustrated in <a href=\"https://youtu.be/DaqqCbmhqVI\" target=\"_blank\">Noah Caldwell-Gervais's review of the game Tyranny</a>, people who are victims of conquest can easily be MADE sufficiently vicious and willing to follow orders, if the conquerors deal with their victims &quot;properly&quot;). In more modern times - when Baali are few and far between, and their enemies numerous and vigilant - a shrewd mind and capacity for subtly are far more important.<br /> <br /> But in all eras, the kind of people Baali tend to go for are not typically nice or constrained by morality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T04:32:10-07:00","id":1415177,"title":"","content":"Just reread this<br /> <br /> I forgot to mention one of the defense lawyers was a Glass Walker, another was a Ventrue ghoul, the prosecutor was a Black Fury Kinfolk and the judge was involved with the Order of Hermes (which was literally like every game line that existed when the real case happened).<br /> <br /> The guy I talked to swears his friend wasn\u2019t kidding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T14:26:55-07:00","id":1415325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1398439-worst-wod-idea-you\u2019ve-ever-heard?p=1411837#post1411837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...But in all eras, the kind of people Baali tend to go for are not typically nice or constrained by morality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except when they do. Baali also have a tendency to embrace people on the opposite end of the morality spectrum, especially religious representatives specifically.<br /> <br /> Problem being, the average Baali isn't going to need to put in much effort to turn a neonate to the dark side, they have the perfect self-fulfilling prophecy for that already: Daimonion 1(Sense Sin).<br /> <br /> I don't think many people have really thought out the full implications of that ability. It gives a person the ability to see all of the worst things anyone around them has thought, their darkest thoughts, and most closely held secrets. All without any of the context or good deeds that would offset the worst perspective you can have of that person. It's giving someone &quot;Detect Evil&quot; in <b>The World of Darkness</b>. It alone is a one-way ticket to slowly alienating everyone around you and quickly degenerating humanity without any help from the storyteller. <br /> <br /> This is also why I think it cheapens the game if storytellers make the baali evil because they're baali or when storytellers mandate random humanity degeneration for having diciplines like daimonion. The discipline is designed to give players and NPCs just enough rope to hang themselves with, something that's much more impactful than &quot;I'm evil now because I got infected with evil-juice #3&quot;.<br /> <br /> For the main discussion that's my vote. The worst ideas in WOD are when they take the shortcut of &quot;infectious evil&quot;&quot; instead of more human characters who are/were destroyed by their own faults and virtues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T15:25:59-07:00","id":1415332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1398439-worst-wod-idea-you\u2019ve-ever-heard?p=1415325#post1415325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except when they do. Baali also have a tendency to embrace people on the opposite end of the morality spectrum, especially religious representatives specifically.<br /> <br /> Problem being, the average Baali isn't going to need to put in much effort to turn a neonate to the dark side, they have the perfect self-fulfilling prophecy for that already: Daimonion 1(Sense Sin).<br /> <br /> I don't think many people have really thought out the full implications of that ability. It gives a person the ability to see all of the worst things anyone around them has thought, their darkest thoughts, and most closely held secrets. All without any of the context or good deeds that would offset the worst perspective you can have of that person. It's giving someone &amp;quot;Detect Evil&amp;quot; in <b>The World of Darkness</b>. It alone is a one-way ticket to slowly alienating everyone around you and quickly degenerating humanity without any help from the storyteller. <br /> <br /> This is also why I think it cheapens the game if storytellers make the baali evil because they're baali or when storytellers mandate random humanity degeneration for having diciplines like daimonion. The discipline is designed to give players and NPCs just enough rope to hang themselves with, something that's much more impactful than &amp;quot;I'm evil now because I got infected with evil-juice #3&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> For the main discussion that's my vote. The worst ideas in WOD are when they take the shortcut of &amp;quot;infectious evil&amp;quot;&amp;quot; instead of more human characters who are/were destroyed by their own faults and virtues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah turning evil because of evil juice is lazy writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T19:58:07-07:00","id":1416669,"title":"","content":"Baali who are not evil. First thing which comes to my mind with this is that everyone defines good and evil at least a bit different; and the definition most Baali had was much more different than most others. It's true that sometimes they got people out of the opposite morale spectrum, but either to corrupt them or because these people were so extreme in their ways that it didn't really make a difference in the end. Chaotic Good people often do many things which might be considered evil by anyone who doesn't have the same believe &amp; value system. Like Inquisitors in the dark ages or Soldiers who really believe in what they do in war for a greater good (or for what they perceive as the greater good),<br /> \u200b<br /> I think that Baali should be mostly &quot;evil&quot;. or to use a better word for it they should be very twisted in their ways and corrupted. Same with any being who does willingly follow / work for major dark forces / the Wyrm / has pacts with (classic) demon overlords (etc.). Warhammer 40k's decription of the chaos taint / corruption is very fitting for this. In the end &quot;evil&quot; is just an infinite source of corruption and each encounter, even small innocent ones with a force will at least put some small seeds of it in the person.<br /> Also the system of mental stability used by Kult &amp; or mental health used by Call of Cthullu might well be used to explain this better then I may do it. <br /> <br /> So no, directly after they got into the Clan Baali don't have to be &quot;evil&quot;. But with the years most of them (like 99.9%) will either get there or be destroyed; most by suicide, because they can't live with their soul getting ever more tainted - and it's not possible to get that kind of taint / mental corruption away. Maybe one is able to suppress it for some years. But it will never go away or even lessen. Also there is the matter of other Baali and their infernal masters who mostly won't tolerate it for a long period of time.. and they ever need more sacrifices. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26345-xithar","name":"Xithar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T23:52:15-07:00","id":1416688,"title":"","content":"But by default, Baali don't follow/work for dark forces or have pacts. Dark Thaumaturgy is not an in-clan discipline for them, and Diamonion is just Valeren's two-eyed cousin if you're not reading a really early version of infernalism that has since been retconned from existence (Demons granted 'demonic' disciplines like malefica in 1e, before all those got sucked into Dark thaumaturgy) <br /> <br /> The only mechanicsm they've got to make them Evil is 'child, do this fucked up shit or i'll destroy you'. If you can escape or kill your sire and the prince doesn't put you to death you can continue on as a regular bloodsucker without anything dragging you towards mustache twirling and torture-porn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-01T21:19:38-08:00","id":1430723,"title":"","content":"-I definitely agree with the 5 point cap in 5th edition Vampire since it makes the lower gen Vampires less special (for lack of a better term) and less of the threat.<br /> -This probably isn't going to win me any friends, but when it comes to v5 Chicago by Night there was one character I would've given a hard pass to. Rowan, the non-binary trans Nosferatu. This character has no plans (except hang out with burners), no schemes, sorta knows one other Vampire, only one workable rumor, and no real personality (other than being proud of being a non-binary trans). Why were they embraced and how do they feel about it (unless being a vamp gave them the genderless body they wanted)? Maybe I'm disappointed that a more interesting Nosferatu like Tammy got killed off to make room for them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T01:53:59-08:00","id":1430732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1398439-worst-wod-idea-you\u2019ve-ever-heard?p=1430723#post1430723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-I definitely agree with the 5 point cap in 5th edition Vampire since it makes the lower gen Vampires less special (for lack of a better term) and less of the threat.<br /> -This probably isn't going to win me any friends, but when it comes to v5 Chicago by Night there was one character I would've given a hard pass to. Rowan, the non-binary trans Nosferatu. This character has no plans (except hang out with burners), no schemes, sorta knows one other Vampire, only one workable rumor, and no real personality (other than being proud of being a non-binary trans). Why were they embraced and how do they feel about it (unless being a vamp gave them the genderless body they wanted)? Maybe I'm disappointed that a more interesting Nosferatu like Tammy got killed off to make room for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same for Let the street run red. One of the Tremere NPC has pretty much no personality outside of being non binary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T06:08:06-08:00","id":1430741,"title":"","content":"I just read Let the Streets Run Red and I don\u2019t remember them, so I guess that proves your point? \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T08:56:55-08:00","id":1430753,"title":"","content":"Bad ideas:<br /> <br /> <b>The whole granola-hippie thing on Mages and Werewolves</b><br /> &quot;<i>Brrr, Science bad, Science makes kills creativity, Scientists hate nature, brrr&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> The whole point of the scientific method is to understand how reality works. If tomorrow we could fly by clapping our hands you would have scientists measuring how many claps, how strong the clap needs to be, for how long it works, if its the motion of the hands or the sound, if you need human-like hands so monkeys/gorillas can fly too, if prosthetic hands are acceptable, etc, and THEN you would have people using that knowledge for traveling, for criminal purposes, rescue missions, etc.<br /> <br /> It felt like a comic book, it was like what a &quot;creative&quot; person thinks that &quot;smart&quot; people behave, and makes no sense... Like reading that Batman is one of the smartest people in the world but does not use all the alien technology (Kryptonian, Thanagarian, everything in the Green Lantern Ring database) that he could access, or that he decided that spending millions in custom made gear/vehicles is a cheaper/faster way to help Gotham than using all possible money for charity, better police salaries/equipment, improving hospitals/sanitation, etc.<br /> <br /> Retconning the Technocracy portrayals as Tradition propaganda, still antagonistic, was very mature.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Consensual reality in Mage</b><br /> &quot;<i>Most people believe in Science, therefore it works and it is KILLING MAGICK</i>,&quot;<br /> <br /> It was not a bad idea <i>per se</i>, but the implementation made the setting lose verisimilitude, &quot;<i>what (most) people believe is reality</i>&quot; makes no sense if you are aware that a vast number of the world inhabitants are superstitious and/or lacking access to technology; more people in America believe in angels and faith healing than in vaccine efficacy; or consider the religiosity of Asia, Africa and Latin America, where the VAST majority of world population is located.<br /> <br /> It showed writers with limited world knowledge, (and I agree with a previous poster that the naming in <i>Mexico City by Night</i> was shameful, a high-school teacher of Spanish could have corrected all the grammatical errors).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Inconsistent mechanics and no crossover compatibility.</b><br /> <i>&quot;Your rules don't apply to me.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I am not talking about power balance, I am talking of things like: a lot of Vampire powers depend on Virtues or Morality, which the other lines do not have; or having potential difficulties above 10, but no clear answer for that scenario (Auto failure? Max difficulty always 10? Extra successes needed?)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf rank increases</b>.<br /> <i>&quot;I must do what society thinks or else.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I read once that Rank was not a power trait, it was the most difficult Status background to raise.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Attributes for Spirits (mainly Rage but others too)</b><br /> <i>&quot;Everyone has an attitude problem.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Makes no sense a Rage attribute for a spirit of peace/libraries/factories, far batter implemented with CofD Rank/Essence/Power/Finesse/Resistance values.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i>WoD: Gypsies</i>, most of <i>Kindred of the East</i> cultural implications, and the usage of the word <i>M\u00e9tis</i></b><br /> Seriously? Even on a decade lacking much in the area of cultural sensibility, those were crass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 01-04-2021, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T19:25:09-08:00","id":1430946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The whole point of the scientific method is to understand how reality works. If tomorrow we could fly by clapping our hands you would have scientists measuring how many claps, how strong the clap needs to be, for how long it works, if its the motion of the hands or the sound, if you need human-like hands so monkeys/gorillas can fly too, if prosthetic hands are acceptable, etc, and THEN you would have people using that knowledge for traveling, for criminal purposes, rescue missions, etc. </div> </div> </div>This is the Order of Hermes. Very much a &quot;Sufficiently Analyzed Magic&quot; group<br /> <br /> The way the TU kind of fucks over actual science is they've created a consensus that generally follows the rules they want and take active steps to sabotage any scientist that starts poking at ideas they don't want explored by cutting their funding, showing up and twisting reality so it doesn't show the results the scientist hopes to prove (thus discrediting them and making future discoveries less likely to be taken seriously) or at the extreme end, killing them. Those scientists might become Etherites if they keep pursuing their theory despite all the prodding to desist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Attributes for Spirits (mainly Rage but others too)</b><br /> <i>&quot;Everyone has an attitude problem.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Makes no sense a Rage attribute for a spirit of peace/libraries/factories, far batter implemented with CofD Rank/Essence/Power/Finesse/Resistance values.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Rage/Gnosis/Willpower are rather poorly named, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T19:59:43-08:00","id":1430948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>angryicecream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1398439-worst-wod-idea-you\u2019ve-ever-heard?p=1430946#post1430946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is the Order of Hermes. Very much a &quot;Sufficiently Analyzed Magic\u201d group</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I wouldn\u2019t say that. The way the Hermetic magic would analyze date would be much more based upon symbolism (as metaphor) and less about causality. That is, they wouldn\u2019t just analyze data and draw theories, they would look at the meanings of actions and the circumstances of a situation and then try to repeat it perfectly, to recreate an effect. For a hermetic, purity of mind and symbolic purpose is more important than probabilities and causal links.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T20:33:37-08:00","id":1430952,"title":"","content":"Suppose it depends on the House. But, yeah, true for a lot if not most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T19:38:24-08:00","id":1431110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>angryicecream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1398439-worst-wod-idea-you\u2019ve-ever-heard?p=1430946#post1430946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The way the TU kind of fucks over actual science is they've created a consensus that generally follows the rules they want and take active steps to sabotage any scientist that starts poking at ideas they don't want explored by cutting their funding, showing up and twisting reality so it doesn't show the results the scientist hopes to prove (thus discrediting them and making future discoveries less likely to be taken seriously) or at the extreme end, killing them. Those scientists might become Etherites if they keep pursuing their theory despite all the prodding to desist.</div> </div> </div> </div>But my next point was that the Consensus thing is poorly defined and/or implemented,<b> as stated in the books</b>, the whole thing does not align to the world at large (neither the real world, nor the world where there is always a missing tribe of magic users somewhere and their associated mortals, independent of splat). I quote myself:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [Consensual reality] was not a bad idea <i>per se</i>, but the implementation made the setting lose verisimilitude, &quot;<i>what (most) people believe is reality</i>&quot; makes no sense if you are aware that a vast number of the world inhabitants are superstitious and/or lacking access to technology; more people in America believe in angels and faith healing than in vaccine efficacy; or consider the religiosity of Asia, Africa and Latin America, where the VAST majority of world population is located. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T19:45:20-08:00","id":1431111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1398439-worst-wod-idea-you\u2019ve-ever-heard?p=1431110#post1431110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But my next point was that the Consensus thing is poorly defined and/or implemented,<b> as stated in the books</b>, the whole thing does not align to the world at large (neither the real world, nor the world where there is always a missing tribe of magic users somewhere and their associated mortals, independent of splat). I quote myself:<br /> <br /> <i>Consensual reality] was not a bad idea </i><i>per se</i><i>, but the implementation made the setting lose verisimilitude, &quot;</i><i>what (most) people believe is reality</i><i>&quot; makes no sense if you are aware that a vast number of the world inhabitants are superstitious and/or lacking access to technology; more people in America believe in angels and faith healing than in vaccine efficacy; or consider the religiosity of Asia, Africa and Latin America, where the VAST majority of world population is located.</i><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in the context of the World of Darkness, which has Vampires, Werewolves, Mages and all sorts of other critters running around in it - this does pretty much match the notion that superstitious masses are still affecting the consensual reality, doesn\u2019t it? <br /> <br /> What it does highlight, however, is how precarious the position of the Technocracy really is. The Mage game (at least in the 1st edition) gave the impression that the Technocracy was almost entirely dominant as an ultra-Modernist force, and the post-modernist Traditions were on the brink of annihilation. The reality is anything but, going on WoD lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T20:02:02-08:00","id":1431114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1398439-worst-wod-idea-you\u2019ve-ever-heard?p=1431111#post1431111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, in the context of the World of Darkness, which has Vampires, Werewolves, Mages and all sorts of other critters running around in it - this does pretty much match the notion that superstitious masses are still affecting the consensual reality, doesn\u2019t it?<br /> <br /> What it does highlight, however, is how precarious the position of the Technocracy really is. The Mage game (at least in the 1st edition) gave the impression that the Technocracy was almost entirely dominant as an ultra-Modernist force, and the post-modernist Traditions were on the brink of annihilation. The reality is anything but, going on WoD lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your point, but mine was even larger, in the World of Darkness, regular faith healing should be the bee's knees in those parts of the world that I mention (including the Bible Belt in USA), and many, MANY other things that would make no sense, if anything the Technocracy should be the ones fighting a losing battle..<br /> <br /> Awakening did a far better job of making a plausible universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T18:55:39-08:00","id":1431237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1398439-worst-wod-idea-you\u2019ve-ever-heard?p=1430732#post1430732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Same for Let the street run red. One of the Tremere NPC has pretty much no personality outside of being non binary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me of one of the example characters in Legacy of Lies who had they/them pronouns despite the game being set in the dark ages. Granted my knowledge of the far east is limited (the character was from there), I know it was pretty patriarchal and probably not that open to people claiming they're neither male nor female and wanting special pronouns. Even if the group accepts the character's pronouns and gender, the rest of the Dark Ages world would be laughing at them at best (it might even be worse if the character was born female). It just makes the character stick out like a sore thumb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T20:15:03-08:00","id":1431247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1398439-worst-wod-idea-you\u2019ve-ever-heard?p=1431114#post1431114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see your point, but mine was even larger, in the World of Darkness, regular faith healing should be the bee's knees in those parts of the world that I mention (including the Bible Belt in USA), and many, MANY other things that would make no sense, if anything the Technocracy should be the ones fighting a losing battle..<br /> <br /> Awakening did a far better job of making a plausible universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Awakening didn\u2019t have a Technocracy in it to try to rationalize everything! <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-07T08:19:51-08:00","id":1431400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1398439-worst-wod-idea-you\u2019ve-ever-heard?p=1431247#post1431247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, Awakening didn\u2019t have a Technocracy in it to try to rationalize everything! </div> </div> </div> </div>I think you misunderstood my point. The problem was not the Technocracy or the Traditions.<br /> <br /> The problem was that the metaphysics of Consensus have no verisimilitude neither in the WoD (as presented in all the gamelines) or our world (as comparison). What most people believe/accept = Consensus, can not happen in WoD with an ascendant Technocracy since most people in WoD do not believe what the Technocracy expounds.<br /> <br /> The real world beliefs of most of the population (half, HALF of US citizens belive that angels are real) are closer to the Traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-07T11:03:52-08:00","id":1431407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1398439-worst-wod-idea-you\u2019ve-ever-heard?p=1431400#post1431400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you misunderstood my point. The problem was not the Technocracy or the Traditions.<br /> <br /> The problem was that the metaphysics of Consensus have no verisimilitude neither in the WoD (as presented in all the gamelines) or our world (as comparison). What most people believe/accept = Consensus, can not happen in WoD with an ascendant Technocracy since most people in WoD do not believe what the Technocracy expounds.<br /> <br /> The real world beliefs of most of the population (half, HALF of US citizens belive that angels are real) are closer to the Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point, I think you are misunderstanding.<br /> <br /> My last post was just a throwaway observation to end the chat with - rather than anything else.<br /> <br /> However, \u2018consensual reality\u2019 has its roots in real world postmodern magical practice and thought - much more so than anything written in Awakening, and is why Mage: The Ascension remains the more interesting game for me, despite all its messiness.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy in the game reflects the growth of secular rationalism and Modernism towards the end of the 20th century, but also historically tracks it back to the Enlightenment. The Traditions in the game however, reflect the rejection of modernism and the paranoia of all sorts of tradition or fringe beliefs that feel persecuted by the rise of secular rationalism and modernism. The rejection of rationalism is basically what postmodernism is about.<br /> <br /> You seem to think that pointing out about the postmodern nature of beliefs around the world undercuts the premise of Mage: The Ascension, but it is actually what the game is about - that reality is not fixed, and that competing world views are competing over what is \u2018truth\u2019 or not. Consensual reality, <i>along with paradigm and paradox</i> are the explanation for how seemingly contradictory world views can exist in the same world. It has complete verisimilitude, because the ideas actually stem from real world concepts.<br /> <br /> The misconception here is that the 'consensual reality\u2019 is a monolithic, fixed entity that cannot incorporate disparate ideas. It isn\u2019t, although the Technocracy want it to be. In terms of the position of the Technocracy standing vs the Traditions and Crafts, it is within the scope of the current game that the Technocracy is in the retreat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 01-07-2021, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T06:48:23-08:00","id":1431465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1398439-worst-wod-idea-you\u2019ve-ever-heard?p=1431400#post1431400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you misunderstood my point. The problem was not the Technocracy or the Traditions.<br /> <br /> The problem was that the metaphysics of Consensus have no verisimilitude neither in the WoD (as presented in all the gamelines) or our world (as comparison). What most people believe/accept = Consensus, can not happen in WoD with an ascendant Technocracy since most people in WoD do not believe what the Technocracy expounds.<br /> <br /> The real world beliefs of most of the population (half, HALF of US citizens belive that angels are real) are closer to the Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm surprised it isn't higher.<br /> <br /> I will readily admit that &quot;What most people believe/accept = Consensus&quot; and is instantly reality is probably the easiest interpretation of how the core introduces the idea of Mage metaphysics, however it is not the only or even the most likely interpretation. The statement 'Consensus defines reality' is on about the same level as 'Every action has an equal and opposite reaction.' It is true but also vague enough that there is more than one way it could work out until you know more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-09T11:22:48-08:00","id":1434959,"title":"","content":"This\u2019uns from White Wolf, itself: Apparently, Asians don\u2019t dream and thus no traditional changelings of any sort exist in the Far East. Asian mythology is FULL of fairytales and mythic tricksters and rampaging monsters a\u2019plenty, But no, apparently the Dreaming in Asia is inert.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-12T07:16:32-08:00","id":1435293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1398439-worst-wod-idea-you\u2019ve-ever-heard?p=1434959#post1434959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This\u2019uns from White Wolf, itself: Apparently, Asians don\u2019t dream and thus no traditional changelings of any sort exist in the Far East. Asian mythology is FULL of fairytales and mythic tricksters and rampaging monsters a\u2019plenty, But no, apparently the Dreaming in Asia is inert.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The General attitude towards Asia in corebooks is full faceplant-into-frozen shit. . It's shitty in Vampire, shitty in werewolf, shitty from the limited material i've seen of mage, screwed in demon.. Wraith, which I'm not big on, presents something interesting but flawed. Now, certain supplement books have done a very good job at salvaging the shit-heaps and making them something good and profound and workable and not-racist, but to find the gold you've got to dig through the shit... Asia shouldn't have it's own unique supernaturals in 90% of cases. It can have it's own politics and philosophy and perhaps some geography-specific resources that aren't getting exported but beyond that... ugh. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 90's americans apparently had really weird ideas. ( I blame a successful post-war Japan). The thing is that today, we can understand east Asia pretty well because there's an abundance of writing and communication between west and east. If the World of Darkness was kickstarted today in this age of internet, they could probably do East asia and south east asia justice (well, this is assuming the OG writers. I doubt we'd get that justice with V5) The problem is Africa, which is like 'the New Asia' in that we know almost enough to be interested but there isn't enough information to actually build a respectful, cohesive and accurate system for -all- of sub-saharan africa, rather than just take very specific pieces from certain places and extrapolate them in the most bizzare and hurtful way. (but also, perhaps in a decade or two, we'll have a much larger share of information and can make sourcebooks for africa) <br /> <br /> Australia's pretty shit too for coverage. But then when I start thinking like this I also think everywhere's pretty shit for WTA; Europe, North America, South america, the middle east... Antartica...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-14T03:13:22-08:00","id":1435434,"title":"","content":"While the research old WW did was quite shit, It's down to the players to actually do some exploration of history, culture and mythology if they want to make their games work properly beyond the tiny bounds that were presented in the original games. With time OP and WW have worked on giving us better frameworks and reminding people to consider the World and the wealth of information we have available nowaday, but the end of the day it's down to us running and playing the games to do our job and treat the people of the world with respect.<br /> <br /> While a lot of the ideas in KotE were downright weird and a mark of their times, there is a interesting game and some brilliant concepts under it, especially if you consider that the Umbra and the local cultures will interpret things differently and be shaped by their own quirks and needs. I do kind of regret the &quot;Asians read...&quot; never got past the introduction for KotE because some of the worst and edgiest crap in the old books is in those pompous introductions. Better yet, KotE quickly started fixing things and making the game world about more than just Japan + a bit of china. It had some of the best splatbooks ever written - Devil Tigers (Oh, My!) and the Companion pretty quickly explained that the vision presented in the core book was limited and that the actuality of the Wan Kuei culture has quite a bit more depth.<br /> <br /> Hengeyokai, while clearly too Japan obsessed, is really not that hard to adapt to a more sensible framework and the Beast Courts are quite an interesting concept if you play up the fact that a Beast Court of India will be different than the one in Malysia, China or in Japan. We never really got a lot of it explained, so it's down to us to actually get it working and incorporate as much culture and history as we can to give it life and do justice to the places we are setting the games in. Heck, it's hard to really mess up much if you don't go into much detail - and compared to all the other factions the core concepts of reality and why things are as they are, are mostly the same between Werewolf and Hengeyokai.<br /> <br /> Wraith, interestingly, decided to play with the whole overfocusing on a single nation. The underlying conflict of Dark Kingdom of Jade is that the Chinese underworld is so powerful that it's trying to subseme and take over all the other places of the dead around them. A lot of the conflict there is distinctly about the cultural oppression and wiping out of identity of the ghosts that don't follow the Yellow Emperor's vision. It's about rebels and survivors trying to keep to their own cultures while being steamrolled by a vast and powerful empire. It resonates with the history of China and is strangely prescient and amazingly fitting for the current times, all things considered.<br /> <br /> I really liked the Hsien, but my knowledge of Changeling is limited. I'm quite confused by the idea that there is no Dreaming there, so will have to read up on it. I always kind of imagined that there would be Changelings in addition to the Hsien considering that their nature is entirely different and that they are less antagonistic than the Wan Kuei/Kindred. I'll have to check out C20 and see what it has to say about it, I got it on a sale but never really read it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Joi